INT. GRAND MERIDIAN HOTEL - 9TH FLOOR CORRIDOR - NIGHT

KIM LARSEN, 30s, wet coat, backs along the wall. Her phone. Dead.

KIM (V.O.)
Eight hours since the flood took the lobby. Nobody warns you the elevators are the first to go.

Emergency lights. Amber. Silence.

KIP LARSEN, 40s, her brother, limps from the stairwell, a fire axe in one hand. Behind him, DETECTIVE SORA NAKAMURA, 50s, drags a bleeding MRS. ODOM, 70s, by the sleeve.

A door SLAMS somewhere below. Water. Rising.

Kim's phone flickers on for one second.

ON PHONE: where r u

Then black again. Nothing.

KIM
Kip, the stairs.

KIP
Kim, the stairs.

^KIM
They're flooded!

KIP
They're flooded!

SORA
Then we go up. The roof.

MRS. ODOM
My knees.

A pipe BURSTS. The lights BUZZ out.

Dark. Breath. Rain.
